<title>UK: Reduced Forties output claims sixth April cargo.</title>
<headline>Reduced Forties output claims sixth April cargo.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A sixth U.K. North Sea Forties cargo was cancelled on Thursday because of lower than expected production at one of the fields feeding Britain's biggest crude stream, oil traders said.</p>
<p>Traders said a cargo due to load April 28-30 would join the list of cancellations on April 14-16, April 17-19, April 18-20, April 20-22 and April 24-26.</p>
<p>Lower than expected output at the North Sea Scott field was responsible for the spate of cancellations which has cut the original April Forties loading programme to 38 cargoes, excluding crude piped straight to the Grangemouth refinery.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
